{SECT 0 {EXCHG {PARA 256 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 16 "IMPORTANT: the  " }
{TEXT 256 7 "shasta " }{TEXT -1 66 " executable must be in your path b
efore you can execute this demo." }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 
50 "To start, we tell maple about the location of the " }{TEXT 258 8 "
shasta.m" }{TEXT -1 31 " file, which is located in the " }{TEXT 259 5 
"maple" }{TEXT -1 139 " directory of shasta.\n Replace the '.' by the \+
appropriate directory on your system. The following line is only valid
 if you are using maple" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 10 "from the  " }
{TEXT 257 5 "maple" }{TEXT -1 105 "  directory of shasta. Alternativel
y, you can add a line to this effect in your .mapleinit file, and then
" }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 24 "run maple from anywhere." }}{PARA 0 "
> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 0 32 "restart; libname := `.`,libname:" }}}{EXCHG 
{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 77 "We then load the shasta interface, bringi
ng the shasta  functions into scope:" }}{PARA 0 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 
0 13 "with(shasta);" }}{PARA 12 "" 1 "" {XPPMATH 20 "6#79%&LoewyG%(adj
ointG%&applyG%*decomposeG%+dispersionG%(efactorG%*eigenringG%.exterior
PowerG%&hyperG%(leftGcdG%(leftLcmG%-makeIntegralG%%multG%*normalizeG%1
polynomialKernelG%3polynomialSolutionG%/rationalKernelG%1rationalSolut
ionG%)rightGcdG%)rightLcmG%.rightQuotientG%)sectionsG%'spreadG" }}}
{EXCHG {PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 93 "Difference operators are entered s
imply as polynomials in the shift and independent variable:" }{TEXT 
-1 0 "" }}{PARA 0 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 0 47 "L := (n+2)*E^2 + (n^2+3*n
+2)*E - n^2 - 3*n - 2;" }}{PARA 11 "" 1 "" {XPPMATH 20 "6#>%\"LG,,*&,&
%\"nG\"\"\"\"\"#F)F))%\"EGF*\"\"\"F)*&,(*$)F(F*F-F)F(\"\"$F*F)F)F,F)F)
F0!\"\"F(!\"$!\"#F)" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 131 "When call
ing a shasta  function, e.g. adjoint, add the shift operator  name and
 independent variable name to the shasta parameters:" }{TEXT -1 0 "" }
}{PARA 0 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 0 21 "tL := adjoint(L,E,n);" }}{PARA 11 
"" 1 "" {XPPMATH 20 "6#>%#tLG,(*&,(*$)%\"nG\"\"#\"\"\"!\"\"F*!\"$!\"#
\"\"\"F0)%\"EGF+F,F0*&,&F(F0F*F0F0F2F0F0F*F0" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "" 0 "
" {TEXT -1 101 "The functions 'polynomialKernel' and  'rationalKernel'
 always  return arrays, potentially empty ones:" }{TEXT -1 0 "" }}
{PARA 0 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 0 22 "rationalKernel(L,E,n);" }}{PARA 11 
"" 1 "" {XPPMATH 20 "6#-%'vectorG6#7\"" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "> " 0 "" 
{MPLTEXT 1 0 28 "K := rationalKernel(tL,E,n);" }}{PARA 11 "" 1 "" 
{XPPMATH 20 "6#>%\"KG-%'vectorG6#7#*&\"\"\"F*%\"nG!\"\"" }}}{EXCHG 
{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 80 "We can verify that the first entry of K i
s indeed a solution of the adjoint of L" }{TEXT -1 0 "" }}{PARA 0 "> \+
" 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 0 19 "apply(tL,K[1],E,n);" }}{PARA 11 "" 1 "" 
{XPPMATH 20 "6#\"\"!" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 139 "Since th
e adjoint of L has a rational solution, L must be reducible, which imp
lies in this case that it must have a hypergeometric solution" }{TEXT 
-1 0 "" }}{PARA 0 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 0 18 "f := hyper(L,E,n);" }}
{PARA 11 "" 1 "" {XPPMATH 20 "6#>%\"fG,&%\"nG!\"\"F'\"\"\"" }}}{EXCHG 
{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 125 "hyper returns either [] if there are no \+
hypergeometric solutions, or f(n) = y(n+1)/y(n) where y is a hypergeom
etric solution." }}{PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 75 "In that case, y can be
 recovered from f by calling rsolve on y(n+1)=f*y(n):" }}{PARA 0 "> " 
0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 0 27 "rsolve(y(n+1)=f*y(n),y(n));" }}{PARA 11 "" 1 "" 
{XPPMATH 20 "6#*()!\"\"%\"nG\"\"\"-%&GAMMAG6#,&F&F'F'F'F'-%\"yG6#\"\"!
F'" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 55 "We could also find that L i
s reducible by factoring it:" }}{PARA 0 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 0 20 "l :
= efactor(L,E,n);" }}{PARA 11 "" 1 "" {XPPMATH 20 "6#>%\"lG-%'vectorG6
#7$,(*&,&%\"nG\"\"\"\"\"#F-F-%\"EGF-F-F,!\"\"!\"#F-,(F/F-F,F-F-F-" }}}
{EXCHG {PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 71 "The above means that L is the prod
uct of those 2 first-order operators." }{TEXT -1 0 "" }}{PARA 0 "> " 
0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 0 24 "L - mult(l[1],l[2],E,n);" }}{PARA 11 "" 1 "" 
{XPPMATH 20 "6#\"\"!" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 146 "It also \+
means that L is not a least common left multiple of first order operat
ors, since 'efactor' always decomposes as an LCLM whenever possible:" 
}{TEXT -1 0 "" }}{PARA 0 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 0 62 "efactor(E^3+(-n-2)
*E^2+(3*n^2+9*n+6)*E-3*n^3-9*n^2-6*n, E, n);" }}{PARA 11 "" 1 "" 
{XPPMATH 20 "6#-%(LeftLcmG6%,&%\"EG\"\"\"*(%\"IGF(-%%sqrtG6#\"\"$\"\"
\"%\"nGF(!\"\",&F'F(F)F(,&F'F(F0F1" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT 
-1 75 "Systems Y(n+1) = A(n)Y(n) are solved by passing the matrix A(n)
 as argument" }{TEXT -1 0 "" }}{PARA 0 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 0 295 "A :
= linalg[matrix](4,4,[(n-1)/(n+5), (7*n^2+4*n+n^3)/(n+5), -n-1, (1-n)*
(n^2+5*n+5)/(n+5),\n        (n-1)/(n*(n+1)*(n+5)), (n-1)/((n+1)*(n+5))
, 0, (n-1)/((n+1)*(n+5)),\n        (n-1)/(n+5), n*(n-1)/(n+5), -n, -(n
^3+3*n^2-5*n-5)/(n+5),\n        (1-n)/(n*(n+5)), (1-n)/(n+5), 1, (n+4)
*(n-1)/(n+5)]);" }}{PARA 11 "" 1 "" {XPPMATH 20 "6#>%\"AG-%'matrixG6#7
&7&*&,&%\"nG\"\"\"!\"\"F-\"\"\",&F,F-\"\"&F-!\"\"*&,(*$)F,\"\"#F/\"\"(
F,\"\"%*$)F,\"\"$F/F-F/F0F2,&F,F.F.F-*&*&,&F-F-F,F.F-,(F5F-F,F1F1F-F-F
/F0F27&*&F+F/*(F,\"\"\",&F,F-F-F-\"\"\"F0\"\"\"F2*&F+F/*&FF\"\"\"F0\"
\"\"F2\"\"!FI7&F**&*&F,F-F+F-F/F0F2,$F,F.,$*&,*F:F-F5F<F,!\"&FUF-F/F0F
2F.7&*&F@F/*&F,\"\"\"F0\"\"\"F2*&F@F/F0F2F-*&*&,&F,F-F9F-F-F+F/F/F0F2
" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 0 27 "K := rationalKernel(A,E
,n);" }}{PARA 11 "" 1 "" {XPPMATH 20 "6#>%\"KG-%'matrixG6#7&7$*&,2*$)%
\"nG\"\"(\"\"\"#\"\"\"\"$W\"*$)F.\"\"'F0#F2\"#;*$)F.\"\"&F0F1*$)F.\"\"
%F0#\"#8\"#[*$)F.\"\"$F0#\"$R#\"#s*$)F.\"\"#F0#\"#6FDF.#FJFDFJF2F0,.F4
F2F9\"\"*F<\"#DFB\"#:FH!#EF.!#C!\"\",$F.#!\"\"\"$?(7$,$*&F0F0,(F<F2FBF
6FH\"\")FTFM\"\"!7$*&,.F9F1F<#F2\"#=FB#FWF8FH#!#<\"#OF.#\"#BFao#FDFJF2
F0,,F<F2FB\"#5FH\"#NF.\"#]\"#CF2FT,&F.FV#F2\"$g$F27$*&,(FH#FWF3F.#FWFi
o#F2FOF2F0,(FHF2F.F6FgnF2FT#F2FX" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 
41 "We can verify that K is indeed a solution" }{TEXT -1 0 "" }}{PARA 
0 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 0 50 "map(normal, evalm(subs(n=n+1,evalm(K)) - \+
A &* K));" }}{PARA 11 "" 1 "" {XPPMATH 20 "6#-%'matrixG6#7&7$\"\"!F(F'
F'F'" }}}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 0 0 "" }}}}{MARK "16 0 0
